Findings, most important first:
1. skills/ue-python/editor-api.md:91-99 is wrong about the toolkit's error check. FUnrealClaudeOutputDevice::Serialize (UnrealClaudeUtils.h:23-27) keeps only the message text, with no 'LogPython: Error:' prefix, and ScriptExecutionManager.cpp:326-376 checks that text. So unreal.log_error('x') does NOT fail a script unless the message itself contains a checked word. 'ErrorWidget' matches none of them (the check looks for 'Error:', not 'Error'); 'KeyErrorHandler' does match. 'An engine error line fails the script' is too strong: it fails only when the line's text contains a checked word. Rewrite these from the source.
2. Class B scope (unreagent-skill-authoring SKILL.md:234-244). ue-python is Class A, and editor-api opens no deferred Class B area, so it is not a Class B skill. But the call table (editor-api.md:34-48) and the bulk-edit example (56-70) document raw unreal.* API nobody has run, and the example is made up. That crosses 'the line you may not cross' and 'do not invent examples that look tested'; an 'untested' label does not cure it. My judgement: keep 'Facts from Epic's page' (sourced to Epic's docs and labelled), the bulk-edit workflow as advice (dry run, one transaction, a count, save, read back) and the pitfalls once corrected; drop the call table and the code example. The alternative is an exception the maintainer records in the skill-authoring rule. That choice is the maintainer's.
3. skills/ue-cpp/project-layout.md:68-69,114-117 recommends BuildSettingsVersion.Latest / EngineIncludeOrderVersion.Latest. The UE 5.8.4 UnrealBuildTool source (Configuration/Rules/TargetRules.cs:174-177,184) warns that Latest 'may cause compatibility issues when upgrading' and carries a 'high risk of introducing compile errors'. The engine's own Templates/TP_Blank/Source/*.Target.cs use V7 / Unreal5_8 (not V5). Have the agent copy the target files from <Engine>/Templates/TP_Blank/Source/ of the installed engine, or name the explicit versions. TP_Blank.Build.cs also adds EnhancedInput.
4. skills/ue-cpp/project-layout.md:121-126: a second module does not need to go into the targets' ExtraModuleNames. UBT's SetupProjectModules (UEBuildTarget.cs:5552-5570, 5.8.4) adds every .uproject module that compiles for the target. Worse, an Editor-type module added to the Game target's ExtraModuleNames breaks package. Say that the .uproject entry is enough.
5. skills/unreagent-iterate/crash-diagnosis.md:20 says 'under 10 s is a startup failure'. That contradicts k208's measurement (a missing project module takes 9-17 s) and this skill's own 5-minute give-up (restarts.md), and an unbuilt plugin module takes about 80 s. Soften or drop it.
6. skills/ue-tasks/failures.md:16 (new row) is exact only for timeout_ms 30000. With a lower timeout_ms, the queue's 60 s CheckTimeouts (MCPTaskQueue.cpp:293-300, 454-475) can cancel the task first, and the result then reads 'Task cancelled during execution'. Mention that.
7. Small fixes: ue-context/SKILL.md:138-139 has two blank lines in a row. unreagent-build/SKILL.md:241-242 has a blank line inside the See also list. unreagent-iterate/SKILL.md:228 was not rewrapped. unreagent-setup/SKILL.md:168-170 'the skills and agents it refreshes (...)' is a fragment, and init counts new/refreshed/unchanged for agents only (init.go:824). ue-cpp/reflection.md:96-101: the list of allowed UPROPERTY types leaves out UObject pointers (TObjectPtr, TWeakObjectPtr), right below the rule that requires them.
